    "updated_at": "2024-04-09T23:27:51Z",
    "body": "One way to create such a signal is `new AbortController().signal` but that does create an object only to have to clean it up. \n\n`new AbortSignal()` throws. In theory that could create a never-aborting signal. Relatedly https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1162 discusses the ideas of subclassing signals, which would likely mean lifting the exception from AbortSignal. ",
